{
  "id": "RAW_cd9fedce",
  "title": "NVIDIA AI 推出 ASPIRE：自改进机器人框架在 LIBERO-Pro 长程任务上实现 31% 零样本性能",
  "url": "https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/07/03/nvidia-ai-introduces-aspire-a-self-improving-robotics-framework-reaching-31-zero-shot-on-libero-pro-long-tasks/",
  "date": "2026-07-04 14:40:16",
  "author": "Asif Razzaq",
  "siteName": "MarkTechPost",
  "content": "<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"h-\">Traditional robot programming is hard to scale. It requires orchestrating multimodal perception, physical contact dynamics, diverse configurations, and execution failures by hand. Code-as-policy systems let language models compose these into executable robot programs. That makes robot behavior inspectable, editable, and debuggable.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">But existing robotic coding agents run in naive execution environments. They receive only coarse, task-level feedback. A failed rollout signals that the task failed, not why. The root cause can be perception, motion planning, grasping, contact dynamics, or long-horizon coordination. These systems also discard fixes once a task ends. So the agent solving its hundredth task is no more experienced than at its first.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A team of researchers from NVIDIA, University of Michigan, UIUC, UC Berkeley, and CMU introduces <strong><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.00272\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">ASPIRE (Agentic Skill Programming through Iterative Robot Exploration)</a></strong>. It is a continual learning system that writes and refines robot control programs. It also distills validated fixes into a reusable, transferable skill library.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-how-aspire-works\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How ASPIRE works</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">ASPIRE runs an open-ended learning loop with three components. It uses a coordinator–actor architecture. A central coordinator manages the shared skill library and dispatches actor coding agents to tasks. Actors do not exchange full chat histories or raw trajectories. Only distilled skills move between them.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Closed-loop robot execution engine</strong>: This replaces coarse rollout feedback with per-primitive multimodal traces. For each perception, planning, and control call, it stores inputs, outputs, and return status. It also stores RGB keyframes, overlays, grasp candidates, object poses, and motion-planning results. The agent inspects only the calls implicated by a failure. It then localizes the fault and validates a repair through re-execution.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Skill library</strong>: Reusable knowledge is rarely an entire task program. So the library stores heterogeneous fixes. These include localization heuristics, perception prompts, grasping constraints, motion primitives, and debugging workflows. Each skill is compact in-context guidance. It holds a failure signature, a when-to-apply condition, a repair strategy, and often a code sketch. The coordinator admits only patterns that pass debug validation and API-policy checks.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Evolutionary search</strong>: Trace-guided debugging alone can collapse into local repair loops. The agent keeps patching the same failed strategy. To broaden exploration, ASPIRE proposes K candidate programs each round. Candidates condition on top-performing prior programs and their remaining failure traces. The next round explores distinct strategies rather than refining one solution.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In simulation, the coding agent is Claude Code with Claude Opus 4.6 and a 1M-token context window. Programs are written in CaP-X, an open-source code-as-policy framework built on MuJoCo Playground. The agent cannot read simulator ground truth. Reading physics-engine state or asset files like <code>.bddl</code>, <code>.xml</code>, or <code>.urdf</code> is forbidden. The rule is simple. If a real robot with a camera could do it, it is allowed.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-interactive-explainer\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Interactive Explainer</strong></h2>\n  <!-- ASPIRE interactive demo — paste into a WordPress \"Custom HTML\" block -->\n  <iframe class=\"lazyload\" id=\"aspire-demo-frame\" height=\"900\" scrolling=\"no\" srcdoc=\"&lt;div id=&quot;aspire-demo&quot;&gt;\n&lt;style&gt;\n#aspire-demo *{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}\n#aspire-demo{\n  font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\n  background:#0a0a0a !important;color:#e6e6e6 !important;\n  border:1px solid #1f1f1f !important;border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;\n  max-width:920px;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.5;\n}\n#aspire-demo .ad-head{padding:18px 20px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#111,#0a0a0a)}\n#aspire-demo .ad-kicker{color:#76B900 !important;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700}\n#aspire-demo .ad-title{font-size:19px;font-weight:700;margin-top:4px;color:#fff !important}\n#aspire-demo .ad-sub{font-size:12.5px;color:#8a8a8a !important;margin-top:5px}\n#aspire-demo .ad-tabs{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:12px 16px 0;background:#0a0a0a}\n#aspire-demo .ad-tab{\n  cursor:pointer;border:1px solid #1f1f1f;background:#111;color:#bdbdbd !important;\n  padding:8px 12px;border-radius:8px 8px 0 0;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;transition:.15s\n}\n#aspire-demo .ad-tab:hover{border-color:#2a2a2a}\n#aspire-demo .ad-tab.on{background:#76B900 !important;color:#0a0a0a !important;border-color:#76B900}\n#aspire-demo .ad-body{padding:18px 20px 8px}\n#aspire-demo .ad-panel{display:none}\n#aspire-demo .ad-panel.on{display:block}\n#aspire-demo h4{font-size:14px;color:#fff !important;margin-bottom:4px}\n#aspire-demo p.ad-note{font-size:12.5px;color:#9a9a9a !important;margin-bottom:12px}\n#aspire-demo canvas{width:100%;background:#0d0d0d;border:1px solid #1a1a1a;border-radius:10px;display:block}\n#aspire-demo .ad-row{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start}\n#aspire-demo .ad-col{flex:1;min-width:240px}\n#aspire-demo .ad-btn{\n  cursor:pointer;background:#76B900 !important;color:#0a0a0a !important;border:none;\n  padding:9px 14px;border-radius:8px;font-weight:700;font-size:12.5px;margin:4px 6px 4px 0\n}\n#aspire-demo .ad-btn.ghost{background:#141414 !important;color:#e6e6e6 !important;border:1px solid #2a2a2a}\n#aspire-demo .ad-btn:active{transform:translateY(1px)}\n#aspire-demo .ad-log{\n  background:#0d0d0d;border:1px solid #1a1a1a;border-radius:10px;padding:10px 12px;\n  font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:11.5px;\n  height:196px;overflow-y:auto;color:#cfcfcf !important\n}\n#aspire-demo .ad-log .ok{color:#76B900 !important}\n#aspire-demo .ad-log .err{color:#ff5d5d !important}\n#aspire-demo .ad-log .dim{color:#6f6f6f !important}\n#aspire-demo .ad-slider{width:100%;accent-color:#76B900;margin:8px 0}\n#aspire-demo .ad-nrow{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:11px;color:#6f6f6f !important}\n#aspire-demo .ad-bars{margin-top:12px}\n#aspire-demo .ad-bar-wrap{margin:10px 0}\n#aspire-demo .ad-bar-label{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:12px;margin-bottom:4px;color:#cfcfcf !important}\n#aspire-demo .ad-bar-track{background:#141414;border-radius:6px;height:22px;overflow:hidden;position:relative;border:1px solid #1a1a1a}\n#aspire-demo .ad-bar-fill{height:100%;border-radius:6px 0 0 6px;transition:width .5s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1)}\n#aspire-demo .ad-fill-a{background:linear-gradient(90deg,#4a7500,#76B900)}\n#aspire-demo .ad-fill-b{background:linear-gradient(90deg,#5a2f6b,#a05bc0)}\n#aspire-demo .ad-baseline{font-size:11px;color:#8a8a8a !important;margin-top:2px}\n#aspire-demo .ad-chips{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:12px}\n#aspire-demo .ad-chip{cursor:pointer;border:1px solid #2a2a2a;background:#111;color:#bdbdbd !important;padding:6px 11px;border-radius:20px;font-size:12px;font-weight:600}\n#aspire-demo .ad-chip.on{background:#76B900 !important;color:#0a0a0a !important;border-color:#76B900}\n#aspire-demo .ad-legend{display:flex;gap:16px;font-size:12px;margin:10px 0 4px;color:#bdbdbd !important;flex-wrap:wrap}\n#aspire-demo .ad-dot{display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:3px;margin-right:5px;vertical-align:middle}\n#aspire-demo .ad-foot{border-top:1px solid #1a1a1a;padding:11px 20px;font-size:11.5px;color:#7a7a7a !important;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px}\n#aspire-demo .ad-foot b{color:#76B900 !important}\n#aspire-demo .ad-src{font-size:11px;color:#6f6f6f !important;margin-top:8px}\n@media(max-width:640px){#aspire-demo .ad-col{min-width:100%}#aspire-demo canvas{height:220px}}\n&lt;/style&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;ad-head&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;ad-kicker&quot;&gt;NVIDIA GEAR · Interactive&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;ad-title&quot;&gt;ASPIRE: how a robot coding agent debugs, then reuses the fix&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;ad-sub&quot;&gt;Three views built from the paper's own numbers. Nothing here reads simulator ground truth.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;ad-tabs&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;ad-tab on&quot; data-tab=&quot;loop&quot;&gt;1 · Debugging Loop&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;ad-tab&quot; data-tab=&quot;lib&quot;&gt;2 · Skill Library → Transfer&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;ad-tab&quot; data-tab=&quot;bench&quot;&gt;3 · Benchmark Explorer&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;ad-body&quot;&gt;\n\n  &lt;!-- PANEL 1 --&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;ad-panel on&quot; data-panel=&quot;loop&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h4&gt;Multi-Angle Approach recovery&lt;/h4&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;ad-note&quot;&gt;The robot must reach the red radio. A direct path enters the table's collision-avoidance buffer, so the planner returns PLANNING_ERROR. ASPIRE rotates the approach vector to find an open side.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;ad-row&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;ad-col&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;canvas id=&quot;ad-canvas&quot; width=&quot;440&quot; height=&quot;300&quot;&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;\n        &lt;div&gt;\n          &lt;button class=&quot;ad-btn&quot; id=&quot;ad-direct&quot;&gt;Try direct approach&lt;/button&gt;\n          &lt;button class=&quot;ad-btn&quot; id=&quot;ad-aspire&quot;&gt;Run ASPIRE repair&lt;/button&gt;\n          &lt;button class=&quot;ad-btn ghost&quot; id=&quot;ad-reset&quot;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;ad-col&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;ad-log&quot; id=&quot;ad-tracelog&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;dim&quot;&gt;trace.json — waiting for a run…&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;!-- PANEL 2 --&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;ad-panel&quot; data-panel=&quot;lib&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h4&gt;Zero-shot transfer scales with library size&lt;/h4&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;ad-note&quot;&gt;Skills accumulated on LIBERO-90 source tasks (N) are reused on held-out LIBERO-Pro Long tasks, with no test-time debugging. Drag N to see success move.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;range&quot; min=&quot;0&quot; max=&quot;3&quot; step=&quot;1&quot; value=&quot;3&quot; class=&quot;ad-slider&quot; id=&quot;ad-nslider&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;ad-nrow&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;N=0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;N=25&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;N=50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;N=90&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:6px;font-size:13px;color:#fff&quot;&gt;Library size &lt;b style=&quot;color:#76B900&quot; id=&quot;ad-nval&quot;&gt;N=90&lt;/b&gt; source tasks&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;ad-bars&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-wrap&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-label&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Position perturbation (Pos)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;ad-posv&quot;&gt;22.6%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-track&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-fill ad-fill-a&quot; id=&quot;ad-posbar&quot; style=&quot;width:22.6%&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;ad-baseline&quot;&gt;CaP-Agent0 baseline: 5.2%&lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-wrap&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-label&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Task / instruction perturbation (Task)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;ad-taskv&quot;&gt;38.3%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-track&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-fill ad-fill-b&quot; id=&quot;ad-taskbar&quot; style=&quot;width:38.3%&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;ad-baseline&quot;&gt;CaP-Agent0 baseline: 2.4%&lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;ad-src&quot;&gt;Values: Table 5, macro-averaged over 10 tasks per axis. N=0 is an empty library.&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;!-- PANEL 3 --&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;ad-panel&quot; data-panel=&quot;bench&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h4&gt;ASPIRE vs the strongest prior baseline&lt;/h4&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;ad-note&quot;&gt;Success rate (%) on held-out seeds. Pick a task. Bars compare ASPIRE against the best-performing prior method on that task.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;ad-chips&quot; id=&quot;ad-benchchips&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;ad-legend&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ad-dot&quot; style=&quot;background:#76B900&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;ASPIRE&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ad-dot&quot; style=&quot;background:#8a4a2a&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;ad-basename&quot;&gt;CaP-Agent0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div id=&quot;ad-benchbars&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;ad-src&quot; id=&quot;ad-benchsrc&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;ad-foot&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;span&gt;Built by &lt;b&gt;Marktechpost&lt;/b&gt; · figures reproduced from the ASPIRE paper (NVIDIA GEAR et al.)&lt;/span&gt;\n  &lt;span&gt;Illustrative interactive · not the official code&lt;/span&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;script&gt;\n(function(){\n  var root=document.getElementById('aspire-demo');\n  // ---- tabs ----\n  var tabs=root.querySelectorAll('.ad-tab'), panels=root.querySelectorAll('.ad-panel');\n  tabs.forEach(function(t){t.addEventListener('click',function(){\n    tabs.forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});\n    panels.forEach(function(p){p.classList.remove('on')});\n    t.classList.add('on');\n    root.querySelector('.ad-panel[data-panel=&quot;'+t.dataset.tab+'&quot;]').classList.add('on');\n    resize();\n  })});\n\n  // ---- PANEL 1: canvas debugging loop ----\n  var cv=root.querySelector('#ad-canvas'), ctx=cv.getContext('2d');\n  var W=440,H=300;\n  var START={x:395,y:150};\n  var robot={x:START.x,y:START.y}, radio={x:200,y:150};\n  var table={x:205,y:70,w:120,h:160};   // solid obstacle just east of the radio\n  var buffer=30;                          // collision-avoidance margin around the table\n  var APPROACH=68;                        // 0.7 m standoff radius (illustrative scale)\n  var log=root.querySelector('#ad-tracelog');\n  var anim=null;\n\n  function clearLog(){log.innerHTML='';}\n  function line(txt,cls){var d=document.createElement('div');if(cls)d.className=cls;d.innerHTML=txt;log.appendChild(d);log.scrollTop=log.scrollHeight;}\n\n  function inBuffer(px,py){\n    return px&gt;table.x-buffer &amp;&amp; px&lt;table.x+table.w+buffer &amp;&amp; py&gt;table.y-buffer &amp;&amp; py&lt;table.y+table.h+buffer;\n  }\n  function drawScene(pathPts,goal,status){\n    ctx.clearRect(0,0,W,H);\n    // table + buffer\n    ctx.fillStyle='#161616';ctx.fillRect(table.x-buffer,table.y-buffer,table.w+buffer*2,table.h+buffer*2);\n    ctx.strokeStyle='#ff5d5d';ctx.setLineDash([4,4]);ctx.strokeRect(table.x-buffer,table.y-buffer,table.w+buffer*2,table.h+buffer*2);\n    ctx.setLineDash([]);\n    ctx.fillStyle='#3a3a3a';ctx.fillRect(table.x,table.y,table.w,table.h);\n    ctx.fillStyle='#6f6f6f';ctx.font='11px monospace';ctx.fillText('collision buffer',table.x-buffer+6,table.y-buffer-6);\n    ctx.fillText('table',table.x+table.w/2-14,table.y+table.h/2+4);\n    // radio\n    ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(radio.x,radio.y,9,0,7);ctx.fillStyle='#ff4d4d';ctx.fill();\n    ctx.fillStyle='#ff8a8a';ctx.fillText('radio',radio.x-14,radio.y-14);\n    // path\n    if(pathPts&amp;&amp;pathPts.length){\n      ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(pathPts[0].x,pathPts[0].y);\n      for(var i=1;i&lt;pathPts.length;i++)ctx.lineTo(pathPts[i].x,pathPts[i].y);\n      ctx.strokeStyle=status==='err'?'#ff5d5d':'#76B900';ctx.lineWidth=2.5;ctx.stroke();ctx.lineWidth=1;\n    }\n    // goal marker\n    if(goal){ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(goal.x,goal.y,6,0,7);ctx.fillStyle=status==='err'?'#ff5d5d':'#76B900';ctx.fill();}\n    // robot\n    ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(robot.x,robot.y,11,0,7);ctx.fillStyle='#e6e6e6';ctx.fill();\n    ctx.fillStyle='#0a0a0a';ctx.font='bold 10px monospace';ctx.fillText('R',robot.x-3,robot.y+4);\n  }\n  drawScene();\n\n  function goalAt(angleDeg){\n    var a=angleDeg*Math.PI/180;\n    return {x:radio.x+APPROACH*Math.cos(a), y:radio.y+APPROACH*Math.sin(a)};\n  }\n  function segCrossesBuffer(a,b){\n    for(var i=0;i&lt;=48;i++){var t=i/48;if(inBuffer(a.x+(b.x-a.x)*t,a.y+(b.y-a.y)*t))return true;}\n    return false;\n  }\n  // build a route that arcs around the collision buffer (like cuRobo planning around it)\n  function routeAround(goal){\n    var start={x:robot.x,y:robot.y};\n    if(!segCrossesBuffer(start,goal)) return [start,goal];\n    var top=Math.max(16,table.y-buffer-18), bot=Math.min(H-16,table.y+table.h+buffer+18);\n    var viaTop=Math.min(start.y,goal.y)-top, viaBot=bot-Math.max(start.y,goal.y);\n    var viaY=viaTop&lt;=viaBot?top:bot;\n    return [start,{x:start.x,y:viaY},{x:goal.x,y:viaY},goal];\n  }\n  function animatePath(pts,cb){\n    if(anim)cancelAnimationFrame(anim);\n    var seg=0,t=0;\n    (function step(){\n      t+=0.045;if(t&gt;1){t=0;seg++;}\n      if(seg&gt;=pts.length-1){var last=pts[pts.length-1];robot.x=last.x;robot.y=last.y;drawScene(pts,last,'ok');if(cb)cb();return;}\n      var a=pts[seg],b=pts[seg+1],cur={x:a.x+(b.x-a.x)*t,y:a.y+(b.y-a.y)*t};\n      robot.x=cur.x;robot.y=cur.y;\n      drawScene(pts.slice(0,seg+1).concat([cur]),pts[pts.length-1],'ok');\n      anim=requestAnimationFrame(step);\n    })();\n  }\n\n  root.querySelector('#ad-direct').addEventListener('click',function(){\n    resetPose();clearLog();\n    line('get_robot_position &amp;rarr; [4.95, 5.04]','dim');\n    line('task: pick up red radio');\n    line('navigate_to_pose &amp;rarr; direct standoff near radio');\n    // naive close goal: a small offset toward the robot, still inside the buffer\n    var d={x:radio.x+22,y:radio.y};\n    drawScene([{x:robot.x,y:robot.y},{x:d.x,y:d.y}],d,'err');\n    line('cuRobo: goal inside collision-avoidance buffer','err');\n    line('PLANNING_ERROR &amp;times;3 &amp;middot; robot stuck &amp;gt;1 m away','err');\n  });\n\n  root.querySelector('#ad-aspire').addEventListener('click',function(){\n    resetPose();clearLog();\n    line('retrieve skill: &lt;span class=&quot;ok&quot;&gt;Multi-Angle Approach&lt;/span&gt;','dim');\n    line('for angle_deg in [180, -90, 90, -45, 45]:');\n    var angles=[180,-90,90,-45,45], chosen=null;\n    for(var i=0;i&lt;angles.length;i++){\n      var g=goalAt(angles[i]);\n      if(!inBuffer(g.x,g.y)){line('&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;ang_'+angles[i]+'&amp;deg; &amp;rarr; clean standoff (0.7 m, far side)','ok');chosen=g;break;}\n      line('&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;ang_'+angles[i]+'&amp;deg; &amp;rarr; inside buffer, skip','dim');\n    }\n    if(chosen){\n      animatePath(routeAround(chosen),function(){\n        line('sample_grasp_pose(red radio) &amp;rarr; 2 candidates');\n        line('grasp_object(arm=0) &amp;rarr; True','ok');\n        line('reward = 1.0 &amp;middot; task_completed = 1','ok');\n        line('&amp;#9733; validated &amp;rarr; admitted as reusable skill','ok');\n      });\n    }else{line('no open side found','err');}\n  });\n\n  root.querySelector('#ad-reset').addEventListener('click',function(){resetPose();clearLog();line('trace.json — waiting for a run…','dim');});\n  function resetPose(){robot={x:START.x,y:START.y};if(anim)cancelAnimationFrame(anim);drawScene();}\n\n  // ---- PANEL 2: library slider ----\n  var LIB=[\n    {n:'N=0', pos:0.0, task:9.4},\n    {n:'N=25',pos:5.6, task:21.8},\n    {n:'N=50',pos:13.8,task:29.2},\n    {n:'N=90',pos:22.6,task:38.3}\n  ];\n  var sl=root.querySelector('#ad-nslider');\n  function updLib(){\n    var d=LIB[+sl.value];\n    root.querySelector('#ad-nval').textContent=d.n;\n    root.querySelector('#ad-posbar').style.width=d.pos+'%';\n    root.querySelector('#ad-taskbar').style.width=d.task+'%';\n    root.querySelector('#ad-posv').textContent=d.pos.toFixed(1)+'%';\n    root.querySelector('#ad-taskv').textContent=d.task.toFixed(1)+'%';\n  }\n  sl.addEventListener('input',updLib);updLib();\n\n  // ---- PANEL 3: benchmark explorer ----\n  var BENCH=[\n    {k:'LIBERO-Pro Object', base:'CaP-Agent0', pairs:[['Pos',98,22],['Task',95,18]], src:'Table 2 · macro-avg over 10 tasks, 50 held-out seeds.'},\n    {k:'LIBERO-Pro Goal', base:'CaP-Agent0', pairs:[['Pos',81,26],['Task',45,17]], src:'Table 2 · macro-avg over 10 tasks, 50 held-out seeds.'},\n    {k:'LIBERO-Pro Spatial', base:'π0.5 / CaP-Agent0', pairs:[['Pos',51,20],['Task',60,14]], src:'Table 2 · strongest prior shown per axis.'},\n    {k:'Robosuite handover', base:'CaP-Agent0', pairs:[['Success',92,20]], src:'Table 3 · two_arm_handover, 100 held-out trials.'},\n    {k:'BEHAVIOR-1K radio', base:'CaP-Agent0', pairs:[['Nav',100,80],['Task',88,56]], src:'Table 4 · 25 held-out seeds, interactive block execution.'}\n  ];\n  var chips=root.querySelector('#ad-benchchips'), barsEl=root.querySelector('#ad-benchbars');\n  var curB=0;\n  BENCH.forEach(function(b,i){\n    var c=document.createElement('div');c.className='ad-chip'+(i===0?' on':'');c.textContent=b.k;\n    c.addEventListener('click',function(){curB=i;chips.querySelectorAll('.ad-chip').forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});c.classList.add('on');drawBench();});\n    chips.appendChild(c);\n  });\n  function drawBench(){\n    var b=BENCH[curB];barsEl.innerHTML='';\n    root.querySelector('#ad-basename').textContent=b.base;\n    root.querySelector('#ad-benchsrc').textContent='Source: '+b.src;\n    b.pairs.forEach(function(p){\n      var wrap=document.createElement('div');wrap.className='ad-bar-wrap';\n      wrap.innerHTML=\n        '&lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-label&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;'+p[0]+' · ASPIRE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;'+p[1]+'%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;'+\n        '&lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-track&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-fill&quot; style=&quot;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#4a7500,#76B900);width:0%&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;'+\n        '&lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-label&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:6px&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;'+p[0]+' · '+b.base+'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;'+p[2]+'%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;'+\n        '&lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-track&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ad-bar-fill&quot; style=&quot;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#5a2f18,#8a4a2a);width:0%&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;';\n      barsEl.appendChild(wrap);\n      var fills=wrap.querySelectorAll('.ad-bar-fill');\n      setTimeout(function(){fills[0].style.width=p[1]+'%';fills[1].style.width=p[2]+'%';},40);\n    });\n    resize();\n  }\n  drawBench();\n\n  // ---- auto-resize ----\n  function resize(){\n    try{var h=root.offsetHeight+40;window.parent.postMessage({aspireDemoHeight:h},'*');}catch(e){}\n  }\n  window.addEventListener('load',resize);setTimeout(resize,300);\n})();\n&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\"></iframe>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-a-worked-example-the-multi-angle-approach-skill\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>A worked example: the Multi-Angle Approach skill</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Consider a BEHAVIOR-1K task where a robot must pick up a radio near a table. Perception returns the radio pose, but repeated <code>navigate_to_pose</code> calls fail. The generated goal lies within about 20 centimeters of the table edge. That falls inside the table’s collision-avoidance buffer, and cuRobo returns PLANNING_ERROR.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The agent reads the trace and localizes the cause. The failure is target infeasibility, not perception or grasping. It then writes a repair that samples standoff poses around the radio.</p>\n  <div class=\"dm-code-snippet dark dm-normal-version default no-background-mobile\" snippet-height=\"\" style=\"background-color:#abb8c3\">\n   <div class=\"control-language\">\n    <div class=\"dm-buttons\">\n     <div class=\"dm-buttons-left\"></div>\n     <div class=\"dm-buttons-right\">\n      <a id=\"dm-copy-raw-code\"><span class=\"dm-copy-text\">Copy Code</span></a>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <pre class=\" no-line-numbers\"><code id=\"dm-code-raw\" class=\" no-wrap language-php\"># radio_pos, safe_navigate() and dist_to() are provided by ASPIRE's robot API\nfor angle_deg in [180, -90, 90, -45, 45]:\n    angle = np.radians(angle_deg)\n    tx = radio_pos[0] + 0.7 * np.cos(angle)      # standoff 0.7 m from the radio\n    ty = radio_pos[1] + 0.7 * np.sin(angle)\n    face_yaw = np.arctan2(radio_pos[1] - ty, radio_pos[0] - tx)\n    moved = safe_navigate([tx, ty, face_yaw], f\"ang_{angle_deg}\")\n    if moved and dist_to(radio_pos[:2]) &lt; 0.8:   # reached a pose within 0.8 m\n        break</code></pre>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Each angle puts the goal on a different side of the object. When one side is blocked, another is often open. Here the 180-degree pose clears the buffer. The validated fix is admitted as a reusable navigation-recovery skill.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-benchmarks-and-results\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Benchmarks and results</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">ASPIRE is evaluated on three benchmark families. LIBERO-Pro tests short-horizon robustness under object, goal, and spatial perturbations. Robosuite covers contact-rich single- and dual-arm manipulation. BEHAVIOR-1K covers long-horizon household mobile manipulation. The primary coding-agent baseline is CaP-Agent0. It uses visual differencing, a predefined skill library, and per-episode test-time retries. The comparison also includes end-to-end vision-language-action policies: OpenVLA, π0, and π0.5.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">On LIBERO-Pro, ASPIRE gains up to 77 points on the Object suite. That figure averages both perturbation axes over the strongest baseline. It also gains 41.5 points on Goal and 42.5 points on Spatial. On Robosuite, bimanual handover rises from 20% to 92%. On BEHAVIOR-1K, the radio pickup task rises from 56% to 88%.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The zero-shot result is notable. Reusing skills accumulated on LIBERO-90, ASPIRE reaches about 31% on held-out LIBERO-Pro Long tasks. Prior methods saturate near 4%.</p>\n  <figure class=\"wp-block-table is-style-stripes\">\n   <table class=\"has-fixed-layout\">\n    <thead>\n     <tr>\n      <th>Dimension</th>\n      <th>End-to-end VLAs (OpenVLA, π0, π0.5)</th>\n      <th>CaP-Agent0</th>\n      <th>ASPIRE</th>\n     </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Paradigm</td>\n      <td>Learned-weight policy</td>\n      <td>Code-as-policy agent</td>\n      <td>Code-as-policy agent</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Cross-task experience</td>\n      <td>None (frozen weights)</td>\n      <td>Discarded after each task</td>\n      <td>Distilled into a skill library</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Failure feedback</td>\n      <td>None at test time</td>\n      <td>Coarse scene-level summaries</td>\n      <td>Per-primitive multimodal traces</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Test-time strategy</td>\n      <td>Direct inference</td>\n      <td>Per-seed reasoning + retries</td>\n      <td>One program per task</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>LIBERO-Pro overall</td>\n      <td>0–13%</td>\n      <td>18%</td>\n      <td>72%</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>LIBERO-Pro Long zero-shot</td>\n      <td>0–5%</td>\n      <td>~4%</td>\n      <td>~31%</td>\n     </tr>\n    </tbody>\n   </table>\n  </figure>\n  <h2 id=\"h-real-robot-skill-transfer\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Real-robot skill transfer</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The research team tests three simulation-discovered skills on a real bimanual YAM station. The real-robot coding agent is OpenAI Codex GPT-5.5. The embodiment and API differ from simulation. Transferred skills reduce debugging cost. Soda-can lifting improved from 13/20 to 19/20 while using about 10x fewer tokens. Drawer opening moved from 0/20 to 11/20, where the no-skill baseline never succeeded.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-key-takeaways\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></h2>\n  <ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n   <li>ASPIRE writes and debugs robot programs, then saves validated fixes as reusable in-context skills.</li>\n   <li>Per-primitive multimodal traces let the agent localize failures instead of guessing from rollout outcomes.</li>\n   <li>It gains up to 77 points on LIBERO-Pro and lifts Robosuite handover from 20% to 92%.</li>\n   <li>Zero-shot transfer reaches about 31% on LIBERO-Pro Long, against about 4% for prior methods.</li>\n   <li>Simulation-discovered skills reduced real-robot debugging cost across a different embodiment and API.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Check out the <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.00272\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><strong>Paper</strong></a> and <a href=\"https://research.nvidia.com/labs/gear/aspire/\"><strong>Project Page</strong></a>.<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Also,&nbsp;feel free to follow us on&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://x.com/intent/follow?screen_name=marktechpost\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark>Twitter</mark></a></strong>&nbsp;and don’t forget to join our&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/machinelearningnews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">150k+ML SubReddit</a></strong>&nbsp;and Subscribe to&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.aidevsignals.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">our Newsletter</a></strong>. Wait! are you on telegram?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://t.me/machinelearningresearchnews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">now you can join us on telegram as well.</a></strong></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Need to partner with us for promoting your GitHu</p>\n  <!-- MOLONGUI AUTHORSHIP PLUGIN 5.2.9 -->\n  <!-- https://www.molongui.com/wordpress-plugin-post-authors -->\n  <!-- CONTENT END 2 -->\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "NVIDIA AI 推出 ASPIRE，一种自改进机器人框架，可从多模态执行轨迹中编写、调试并蒸馏可复用的机器人控制技能，在长程 LIBERO-Pro 任务上实现 31% 的零样本性能。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "NVIDIA AI 推出 ASPIRE，一种自改进机器人框架，可从多模态执行轨迹中编写、调试并蒸馏可复用的机器人控制技能，在长程 LIBERO-Pro 任务上实现 31% 的零样本性能。",
  "summary": "ASPIRE 是一种面向机器人编程智能体的持续学习系统，解决了现有代码即策略方法在每次任务后丢弃经验、仅接收粗粒度失败反馈的局限。该框架采用协调器-执行器架构，包含三个核心组件：闭环机器人执行引擎，用于捕获每个原语的多模态轨迹（RGB 关键帧、抓取候选、运动规划结果）；技能库，将异构经验证修复存储为紧凑的上下文引导；以及进化搜索机制，每轮生成 K 个候选程序以避免局部修复循环。在 LIBERO-Pro、Robosuite 和 BEHAVIOR-1K 上的评估显示，ASPIRE 实现了显著提升，包括在 LIBERO-Pro Object 套件上提升 77 个百分点，以及在长程任务上实现 31% 的零样本性能，而此前方法仅约 4%。该系统还展示了向双臂 YAM 工位的真实机器人技能迁移，其具身形态和 API 均不同，调试成本降低约 10 倍。",
  "mainPoints": [
    {
      "point": "ASPIRE 以逐原语多模态执行轨迹替代粗粒度任务级反馈",
      "explanation": "闭环引擎为每次感知、规划和控制调用存储输入、输出及返回状态，实现精确的失败定位，而非从 rollout 结果中猜测。"
    },
    {
      "point": "经验证修复被蒸馏为可复用、可迁移的技能库",
      "explanation": "与丢弃经验的先前系统不同，ASPIRE 将异构修复——定位启发式、感知提示词、抓取约束——存储为带有失败签名和应用条件的紧凑上下文技能。"
    },
    {
      "point": "K 候选进化搜索避免局部修复循环",
      "explanation": "每轮基于表现最优的先前尝试和剩余失败轨迹生成多个程序，探索不同策略而非对单一失败方案进行微调。"
